6,A Language Isolate in New Mexico - Keres - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ybG79PXzub4,"Jan 22, 2022 · Keres Language Loss in the Santo Domingo Pueblo Community. University of New Mexico. Sean Calvert, Alyssa Donohue, Stephen Donohue, Karen McDonald. 2013. Preserving the Keres Language and... What language do the Keres people speak? The Keres people are one of the Pueblo peoples. They speak English, Keresan languages, and in one pueblo Keresan Sign Language. The seven Keres pueblos are: The western pueblos, Acoma and Laguna, are the largest by area. Abronia fragrans – The Keres people mix ground roots of the plant with corn flour, and eat to gain weight. Is Keres a Native American language? Keres (/ ˈkeɪreɪs /), also Keresan (/ ˈkɛrəsən /), is a Native American language, spoken by the Keres Pueblo people in New Mexico. Depending on the analysis, Keres is considered a small language family or a language isolate with several dialects. What is Keresan language? Baanaʼa, egu kauʼseeʼe, atsi sʼaama-ee srayutse. Keresan is a split-ergative language in which verbs denoting states (i.e. stative verbs) behave differently from those indexing actions, especially in terms of the person affixes they take. How many people speak Keres? According to the UNESCO Atlas of the World's Languages in Danger, there are 13,190 speakers of both the Eastern and Western dialects of Keres. The language is classified as definitely endangered. An overview of the Acoma Language Program (Part of the Acoma Department of Education) at the Acoma Pueblo.","Keres, Eastern",Keresan
7,"Keres, Eastern | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kee/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..fwsYs0g4EuYcwMqJsZ91wprXooWOGJ-8CVmai_wl_hk,Eastern Keres is an endangered indigenous language of the United States. It belongs to the Keresan language family.,"Keres, Eastern",Keresan
8,Keres language Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Keres_language,"Contents. Keresan Language Groups. Eastern Keres Speakers.Traditional Keresan beliefs say that Keres is a sacred language. It should only be spoken, not written. Also, the Pueblo people faced persecution for their religion in the past.","Keres, Eastern",Keresan
